# Simple change to svunit_string_utils.svh to clean up VCS Warning-[IASC] Illegal argument in string comparison

- Source URL: https://github.com/svunit/svunit/issues/193

When using the latest SVUnit with VCS Version S-2021.09-SP2-4
I get this warning which makes you do a double take each time you run tests:

Warning-[IASC] Illegal argument in string comparison
/proj/ccd_func_dev0/users/craftsmanship/repos/svunit/svunit_base/svunit_string_utils.svh, 17
svunit_pkg, "s[i]"
  Either string or string literal is expected as first argument to the string 
  comparison operation.
  Use the string cast operator to convert it to a string literal.


The fix is this:
iff --git a/svunit_base/svunit_string_utils.svh b/svunit_base/svunit_string_utils.svh
index 2b2e5b4..b1a437b 100644
--- a/svunit_base/svunit_string_utils.svh
+++ b/svunit_base/svunit_string_utils.svh
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
     for (int i = 0; i < s.len(); i++) begin
       if (i == s.len()-1)
         parts.push_back(s.substr(last_char_position+1, i));
-      if (s[i] == char) begin
+      if (string'(s[i]) == char) begin


